course: dictionary
lesson: 768
title: Same word, different job
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. You can find the right one by reading the words around it, which are its context. Beanbag is a good example: it can be a big soft chair or a small bag for games.
explain: «Kai laughed so much he fell off his beanbag.» You fall off a chair, not a bag of beans, so here a beanbag is the big soft chair. Try swapping in chair: "he fell off his chair" still makes sense, so chair is the right meaning.
explain: «The teacher sat them on the same squashy beanbag.» Squashy tells you the beanbag is soft, which fits a comfy chair. In PE, a beanbag is the small cloth bag you throw and catch, so always check which job fits the sentence.
fact: A beanbag is a large soft bag filled with small plastic balls, used as a comfy chair.
fact: A small beanbag is a cloth bag filled with dried beans or rice, used for throwing and catching in games.
fact: Beanbag chair and beanbag toss are phrases that use the word in these two ways.
fact: «Squashy» means soft and easy to squash, so it describes how the beanbag feels.
fact: Context clues, such as falling off or throwing, help you choose the right meaning of a word.
exercise: «Kai laughed so much he fell off his beanbag.» What is the beanbag here? | A cloth bag for throwing in games | A bag of dried beans to cook | *A big soft chair to sit on | A tin for keeping biscuits
exercise: In PE, the teacher says, "Balance the beanbag on your head." What is a beanbag here? | A cushion for the floor | A rubber ball for football | *A small cloth bag, used in PE for balancing and throwing | A bean that grows in a garden
exercise: Find and copy one word from «the teacher sat them on the same squashy beanbag» that tells you how soft the beanbag is. | teacher | sat | *squashy | same
test: Which meaning fits a beanbag used in a toss game? | A tin of biscuits | A large soft chair filled with plastic balls | A cushion for a bed | *A small cloth bag filled with dried beans or rice
test: Maddie and Lily sat on a squashy beanbag on their first day. What does the word tell you about it? | It was very hard and cold | It was a bag for throwing in a game | *It was a soft chair for sitting | It was filled with water
exam: Which phrase names a game where you throw something? | beanbag chair | *beanbag toss | squashy beanbag | soft beanbag
